million viewers and earning season is still asking how those same rate sensitive

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:51.105
sectors trade under split control in Washington. Eritzia ticker ATZ on the TSX is

00:01:51.105 --> 00:01:57.125
up 519% over three years, and the Motley Fool Canada frames that run as the reason to

00:01:57.125 --> 00:02:03.045
park the next doubling inside a tax-free savings account, or TFSA, where a future gained

00:02:03.045 --> 00:02:06.065
does not meet the capital gains inclusion rate on the way out.

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:11.205
Think of the TFSA as a backyard greenhouse with the tax collector locked outside.

00:02:11.845 --> 00:02:16.365
Every extra tomato stays on your side of the glass, which is the whole point when a name

00:02:16.365 --> 00:02:17.445
is still trying to double.

00:02:18.085 --> 00:02:24.865
Canadian's born in 1991 or earlier already hold $109,000 of accumulated contribution room,

00:02:25.225 --> 00:02:29.465
enough to concentrate in a high-growth name without inventing room you do not have.

00:02:30.045 --> 00:02:34.865
The account is the simplest registered wrapper to use because investment income earned inside it

00:02:34.865 --> 00:02:40.885
stays tax-free and withdrawals carry no tax liability, which is why the largest growth bets

00:02:40.885 --> 00:02:44.785
belong there, rather than in a taxable account that would clip a later double.

00:02:44.785 --> 00:02:48.545
Open the TFSA at WealthSimple or Questrade.

00:02:49.105 --> 00:02:52.185
I have no financial relationship with WealthSimple or Questrade.

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:59.345
Then screen for 5-year revenue growth above 15% and market caps under $10 billion, and

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:03.325
size the position so it fits the room the contribution tracker already shows.

00:03:04.045 --> 00:03:08.665
Aurezia beat its own 5-year growth targets a year early and still aims to double again

00:03:08.665 --> 00:03:13.805
over the coming 5 years, which is exactly the kind of second act this structure is built

00:03:13.805 --> 00:03:19.705
to shield. The approach works when the stock delivers multi-bagger returns. It fails if the name

00:03:19.705 --> 00:03:26.005
enters a prolonged drawdown, because a loss inside the TFSA cannot be harvested against gains elsewhere.

00:03:26.645 --> 00:03:32.705
A registered retirement savings plan, or RRSP, still delivers an immediate deduction that can drop

00:03:32.705 --> 00:03:37.905
a peak earner into a lower bracket, so the two accounts complement each other rather than compete.

00:03:37.905 --> 00:03:44.585
growth concentrated in the TFSA, deduction harvested in the RRSP during high-earning years,

00:03:45.005 --> 00:03:50.085
though RRSP withdrawals count as income and can pressure old age security or OAS,

00:03:50.785 --> 00:03:52.745
once they clear the clawback thresholds.

