The full history since March 2026 is 95 trades, a 50% win rate, and cumulative P&amp;L of minus

00:09:23.704 --> 00:09:30.504
is $28.13. The rules are still testing whether a named invalidation and a preset stop can

00:09:30.504 --> 00:09:35.364
turn that small negative alpha, and the next measurement is whatever interflex does against

00:09:35.364 --> 00:09:41.973
the NASDAQ over its own five sessions. Semiconductor names sitting in a TFSA have already dropped

00:09:41.973 --> 00:09:53.313
31.30% over three months. The paper value at $475.88, after a $216.87 loss, and a market order

00:09:53.313 --> 00:09:56.153
to exit at the open is where the real damage hides.

00:09:56.813 --> 00:10:00.533
The fill is set by the bid-ask spread and order book depth in that minute.

00:10:01.033 --> 00:10:03.593
Not by the last traded price still printed on the chart.

00:10:04.173 --> 00:10:08.733
And when news hits, that spread can gap from a few cents to 15 or 20 cents in the first

00:10:08.733 --> 00:10:12.913
30 minutes, which is the difference between the exit you planned and the one you get.

00:10:13.493 --> 00:10:17.613
Picture the last sale on a chart as the price of the house that sold down the street last

00:10:17.613 --> 00:10:17.973
week.

00:10:18.473 --> 00:10:22.773
Useful gossip, not the bid the buyer standing in your driveway will actually honor this

00:10:22.773 --> 00:10:27.853
morning. Set a limit at the midpoint of the live spread and refresh it every 60 seconds

00:10:27.853 --> 00:10:32.853
instead of handing the open to a market order, because a clean pattern on the daily chart is a

00:10:32.853 --> 00:10:38.813
zone, not a promise of an orderly print. Losses inside the TFSA stay trapped there and cannot

00:10:38.813 --> 00:10:44.293
offset gains in another account, so a sloppy fill on a name that has already fallen this hard is

00:10:44.293 --> 00:10:49.453
capital you do not get to use again, which is why the exit mechanic matters more than the picture

00:10:49.453 --> 00:10:55.473
of support. The misconception is that a tidy chart guarantees a tidy fill. The fix is to treat

00:10:55.473 --> 00:11:00.833
every technical level as a probability zone, and to let the live book, not yesterday's close,

00:11:01.413 --> 00:11:06.781
set the price you will actually take. Sort the TFSA by three-year total return,

00:11:07.341 --> 00:11:13.321
flag any name up more than 300% and write down its current weight so next week you can decide whether

00:11:13.321 --> 00:11:19.561
it still deserves that much room before contribution room resets. Before we wrap, watch whether energy

00:11:19.561 --> 00:11:24.741
services volume confirms that the next session is open because that is the missing third factor

